    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d397">

                <pb facs="0401" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg389"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">874.00/11–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States Representative in Bulgaria</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Barnes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sofia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-11-19T15:00:00+02:00">November 19,
                            1945—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 20—11:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>703. In acknowledging today receipt of Mr. Stainov’s note, text of which
                    transmitted mytel 700, November 17, 1 conveyed to MinFonAff <pb facs="0402"
                        n="390" xml:id="pg390"/> contents Department’s tel 375, November 17<anchor
                        n="14" xml:id="d397-f1"/> to make sure that accurate report of what was said
                    to General Stoichev by Under Secretary of State reaches Bulgarian
                    authorities.</p>
                <p>I am repeating this to Moscow as 319 and suggest that Department repeat its 375
                    also.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Barnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
